@book{bouchard_building_2024,
 abstract = {Leverage Amazon Bedrock and other AWS services to accelerate the development of generative AI applications

Key Features
• Find the right generative AI use cases for your business with real-world examples
• Build generative AI applications using Amazon Bedrock and other AWS services
• Implement full-stack generative AI applications on AWS with code examples

Book Description
AWS is recognized and trusted as a platform that offers a highly reliable and scalable solution for machine learning applications. The book begins with an introduction to generative AI, followed by a discussion of the AWS ecosystem and the services it offers. You'll then implement a Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) solution using Amazon Bedrock and Amazon OpenSearch Service. Next, you'll explore advanced techniques such as fine-tuning and evaluation of generative AI models. As you advance, you'll learn how to build multimodal applications by integrating Amazon Bedrock with other AWS services such as Amazon Rekognition and Amazon Transcribe. You'll also learn how to deploy and monitor your generative AI applications using Amazon SageMaker and Amazon CloudWatch. By the end of this book, you'll have the knowledge and skills needed to build and deploy generative AI applications on AWS.

What you will learn
• Understand the fundamentals of generative AI and its applications
• Set up your development environment for generative AI on AWS
• Implement RAG solutions using Amazon Bedrock and Amazon OpenSearch Service
• Fine-tune and evaluate generative AI models
• Build multimodal generative AI applications
• Deploy and monitor generative AI applications on AWS

Who this book is for
This book is for solution architects, machine learning engineers, and developers who want to build and deploy generative AI applications on AWS. It will also be useful for anyone interested in learning about generative AI and its applications on AWS. A basic understanding of AWS services and machine learning concepts is required.},
 abstract_lang = {en},
 abstract_source = {x-ai/grok-4-fast},
 annote = {Query date: 2025-10-25 20:50:36},
 author = {Bouchard},
 keywords = {source: Google Scholar},
