 abstract = {This paper proposes a novel federated learning framework for privacy-preserving anomaly detection in industrial IoT networks. By integrating differential privacy mechanisms with graph neural networks, the approach enables collaborative model training across distributed edge devices without sharing raw data. Experimental results on benchmark datasets demonstrate superior detection accuracy and reduced communication overhead compared to traditional centralized methods. The framework addresses key challenges in scalability and security for real-world deployment in smart manufacturing environments.},
