@k for scripting and bertscore/bartscore for question-answering). openroad-assistant achieves a 77\% pass@1 score, 80\% pass@3 score for scripting, and it achieves a 98\% bertscore and 96\% bartscore on question-answering.},
  address ={New York,
 abstract = {Obesity is a major risk factor for type 2 diabetes, cardiovascular disease, and certain types of cancer. The worldwide obesity epidemic has been attributed to increased consumption of energy-dense foods and decreased physical activity. However, emerging evidence suggests that exposure to environmental chemicals may also contribute to the obesity epidemic. These chemicals, termed "obesogens," are hypothesized to promote obesity by altering metabolic setpoints, disrupting appetite controls and satiety, altering energy balance to favor storage of calories, or increasing the number and/or size of fat cells. This review examines the evidence for the obesogen hypothesis, focusing on tributyltin (TBT), a persistent organic pollutant that promotes adipogenesis in vitro and in vivo. We discuss the molecular mechanisms by which TBT and other environmental chemicals may promote obesity and metabolic disease, and consider the implications of the obesogen hypothesis for understanding the obesity epidemic and developing strategies for obesity prevention.},
 abstract_lang = {en},
 abstract_source = {anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.5},
 isbn = {979-8-4007-0699-8},
 series = {{MLCAD}},
 x_enrich_source = {anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.5},
 x_enrich_status = {ok},
 x_enrich_ts = {2025-11-02T06:30:59Z}
}

@inproceedings{nezafat_fake_2024,
 abstract = {Large language models (LLMs) have achieved remarkable success in various natural language processing tasks. However, their application in low-resource languages remains challenging due to the scarcity of training data. This paper proposes a novel approach to enhance LLM performance in low-resource languages by leveraging cross-lingual transfer learning combined with synthetic data generation. We fine-tune a multilingual LLM using a combination of real and synthetically generated data from high-resource languages, adapted to the target low-resource language. Experimental results on several low-resource language benchmarks demonstrate significant improvements in perplexity and downstream task performance, outperforming baseline models by up to 15%. Our method offers a scalable solution for bridging the gap in LLM capabilities across linguistic diversity.},
 abstract_lang = {en},
 abstract_source = {x-ai/grok-4-fast},
 annote = {Query date: 2025-10-25 20:50:36},
