 abstract = {This study investigates the effects of climate change on coastal ecosystems in the Mediterranean region. Using a combination of satellite imagery and field data collected from 2010 to 2020, we analyze changes in vegetation cover, sea level rise, and biodiversity loss. Results indicate a 15% decline in mangrove populations due to increased salinity and temperature. Policy recommendations include enhanced monitoring and restoration efforts to mitigate further degradation.},
