 abstract = {This study investigates the antimicrobial properties of essential oils extracted from various medicinal plants against common pathogenic bacteria. Methods included disk diffusion assays and minimum inhibitory concentration determinations. Results showed significant inhibitory effects, particularly from oregano and thyme oils, suggesting potential applications in natural antimicrobial agents. The findings highlight the need for further in vivo studies to validate these effects.},
